Test the restart after a change of devices

WebRTC patch 0016 has the echo controller aligned again at the first start of recording
after a change of audio devices, forgetting only its transparent mode
(EchoControl::RestartForOtherDevices), where patch 0011 made it anew; a change a device's
own restart already handled while recording ran is not taken again. In
test/echo_call.test.cc the echo controller counts its restarts for other devices. A change
while the microphone is off, one while recording runs with no device restart, one before
a failed start and one as the sound server goes (the start the device keeps for later)
restart it at the next start in the call as a restart for other devices; the next unmute
with no change is a plain restart. In the test of patch 0014, a device restart after a
change is a plain restart, the unmute after it too (the change handled once), and a newer
change while the microphone is off a restart for other devices. A change and a device
restart marked while recording is stopped, with the first recorded block reaching the
audio processing before the audio state's start of recording returns (the mock device
delivers it from its start), still give the unmute's restart for other devices. The
helper for an unmute no longer expects a new controller after a change marked by
another test's device module.

